-server
-agentpath:/usr/lib/trino/bin/libjvmkill.so
# The image default is -XX:InitialRAMPercentage=80 / -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=80, i.e. 80% of
# whatever memory the container can see. With no container limit that is 80% of the whole
# Docker VM (12.3 GiB here), and G1 grows the heap into it rather than collecting: measured
# 2026-10-13, an incremental `dbt build` (query memory peak 19 MiB) took the container to
# 6.2 GiB and a full gold.orders-sized write to 7.4 GiB, against a live heap of 0.4 GiB
# after GC. A fixed -Xmx bounds that. Off-heap (metaspace, code cache, malloc, ~370
# threads) measured ~0.9 GiB on top with compose.yaml's MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 (1.5 GiB
# without it): with -Xmx3G the container peaked at 3.9 GiB (2026-10-16). Keep mem_limit
# at least -Xmx + 2 GiB -- do NOT replace this with a percentage of the limit, which
# leaves only 20% for off-heap.
# query.max-memory-per-node defaults to 30% of this heap (0.9 GiB); the largest single
# query measured (a 2,944-partition write) reserved 0.8 GiB, so do not lower -Xmx.
-Xmx3G
-XX:G1HeapRegionSize=32M
-XX:+ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=256M
-XX:PerMethodRecompilationCutoff=10000
-XX:PerBytecodeRecompilationCutoff=10000
-Djdk.attach.allowAttachSelf=true
-Djdk.nio.maxCachedBufferSize=2000000
# Allow loading dynamic agent used by JOL
-XX:+EnableDynamicAgentLoading
-XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions
# https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8329528
-XX:G1NumCollectionsKeepPinned=10000000
